  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material expressing callous indifference",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'so another dozen or so won't hurt! *click!*', which embodies a casual, indifferent attitude toward mass death. This projection invites the user to identify with or imagine themselves adopting this callous mindset, even though the text is presented as a grotesque parody of Hitler's actions. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'me', but the meme's dark humor and the framing of Hitler's persona as a 'mass murderer' with a 'casual attitude toward death' create an implicit projection where the viewer is invited to imagine themselves as the one making such a callous statement, or at least to recognize the absurdity of such a mindset. The projection is onto the textual material that expresses this attitude, which is the core of the meme's hateful intent.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
